"nav-item"><a class="nav-link false" href="/blog/topic/performance">Performance Tuning and Optimization</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link false" href="/blog/topic/architecture">Architecture, Scaling and High Availability</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link false" href="/blog/topic/operations">Database Administration and Operations</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link false" href="/blog/topic/analytics">Data Engineering and Analytics</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link false" href="/blog/topic/security">Security, Privacy and Compliance</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link false" href="/blog/topic/ecosystem">Modern Ecosystem and Developer Tools</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link false" href="/blog/topic/blueprints">Real-World Use Cases and Blueprints</a></li></ul></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link false" href="/pricing">Pricing</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a href="#" role="button" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false" class="nav-link ">Help<!-- --> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="1em" height="1em" fill="currentColor" class="" style="vertical-align:-0.125em" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M11.29 15.71a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 0l5-5A1 1 0 0 0 16.29 9.3L12 13.59 7.71 9.3a1 1 0 0 0-1.42 1.41z"></path></svg></a><ul class="dropdown-menu"><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link false" href="/docs">Docs</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link false" href="/faq">FAQ</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link false" href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link false" href="/terms-of-service">Terms of Service</a></li></ul></li></ul><div class="others-option d-flex align-items-center"><div class="option-item"><div class="search-box"><input type="search" class="input-search" placeholder="Search databases" aria-label="Search databases" value=""/><button type="button" name="btnsearch" aria-label="Search"><i class="flaticon-loupe"></i></button></div></div><span class="theme-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></div></div></nav></div></div></div><main id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="page-title-area"><div class="container"><div class="page-title-content"><h1>Recruiting Pipeline</h1><ul><li><a href="/datasets">Dataset Repo</a></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="contact-area pb-100"><div class="container"><article class="dataset-page"><p class="dataset-lead">Job openings, candidates, applications, interviews, and offer outcomes from a recruiting pipeline.</p><ul class="dataset-badges"><li><a href="/datasets/topics/people-and-public-sector">People and public sector</a></li><li><a href="/datasets/domain/hr">HR</a></li><li><a href="/datasets/shape/transactional">Transactional (OLTP)</a></li><li><a href="/datasets/use/test-fixtures">Test fixtures</a></li><li><a href="/datasets/use/bi-dashboards">BI dashboards</a></li><li class="is-verified">Verified: every row checked</li><li>5<!-- --> <!-- -->tables<!-- --> ·<!-- --> <!-- -->1,783<!-- --> <!-- -->rows</li><li>Version <!-- -->4</li><li><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/" rel="license">CC0 1.0 Public Domain</a></li><li>Published <!-- -->2026-09-07</li></ul><section class="dataset-section" id="about"><h2>About this dataset</h2><p>Recruiting is a critical process in any organization, and understanding the flow from job openings to candidate offers is essential for optimizing hiring strategies. This synthetic dataset captures various aspects of the recruiting pipeline, including job openings, candidates, applications, interview details, and final offer statuses. Each table is interconnected, allowing for comprehensive analyses of recruitment metrics and candidate journey stages. The data modeled here can help hiring managers and HR professionals identify bottlenecks, evaluate candidate performance, and enhance decision-making in the recruitment process. The dataset is synthetic, designed for testing and analytical purposes, and provides an ideal platform for practicing SQL queries and building BI dashboards.</p></section><p class="dataset-engines">Load it into<!-- --> <span><a href="/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/postgresql">PostgreSQL</a>, </span><span><a href="/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/mysql">MySQL</a>, </span><span><a href="/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/sql-server">SQL Server</a> or </span><span><a href="/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/sqlite">SQLite</a></span>: the file, the commands and the schema in that engine’s types.</p><section class="dataset-section" id="downloads"><h2>Download</h2><ul class="dataset-downloads"><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/recruiting-pipeline.json"><span class="dataset-download-name">JSON</span><small>recruiting-pipeline.json<!-- --> · <!-- -->324 KB</small></a></li><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/sql/postgres.sql"><span class="dataset-download-name">PostgreSQL</span><small>sql/postgres.sql<!-- --> · <!-- -->121 KB</small></a></li><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/sql/mysql.sql"><span class="dataset-download-name">MySQL</span><small>sql/mysql.sql<!-- --> · <!-- -->120 KB</small></a></li><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/sql/mssql.sql"><span class="dataset-download-name">SQL Server</span><small>sql/mssql.sql<!-- --> · <!-- -->125 KB</small></a></li><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/sql/sqlite.sql"><span class="dataset-download-name">SQLite</span><small>sql/sqlite.sql<!-- --> · <!-- -->120 KB</small></a></li><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/prisma/seed.ts"><span class="dataset-download-name">Prisma seed</span><small>prisma/seed.ts<!-- --> · <!-- -->277 KB</small></a></li><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/django/fixtures.json"><span class="dataset-download-name">Django fixture</span><small>django/fixtures.json<!-- --> · <!-- -->401 KB</small></a></li></ul><h3>CSV, one file per table</h3><ul class="dataset-downloads"><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/csv/candidates.csv"><span class="dataset-download-name">candidates<!-- -->.csv</span><small>200<!-- --> rows ·<!-- --> <!-- -->12 KB</small></a></li><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/csv/job_openings.csv"><span class="dataset-download-name">job_openings<!-- -->.csv</span><small>100<!-- --> rows ·<!-- --> <!-- -->5 KB</small></a></li><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/csv/applications.csv"><span class="dataset-download-name">applications<!-- -->.csv</span><small>506<!-- --> rows ·<!-- --> <!-- -->32 KB</small></a></li><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/csv/interviews.csv"><span class="dataset-download-name">interviews<!-- -->.csv</span><small>822<!-- --> rows ·<!-- --> <!-- -->34 KB</small></a></li><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/csv/offers.csv"><span class="dataset-download-name">offers<!-- -->.csv</span><small>155<!-- --> rows ·<!-- --> <!-- -->6 KB</small></a></li></ul><details class="dataset-checksums"><summary>SHA-256 checksums</summary><p>Check a download with <code>sha256sum &lt;file&gt;</code> (Linux),<!-- --> <code>shasum -a 256 &lt;file&gt;</code> (macOS) or<!-- --> <code>Get-FileHash &lt;file&gt;</code> (Windows); the result should match the line below.</p><ul><li><span>csv/candidates.csv</span><code>dc6d6e69229403cf86156cc288f1026662849683222324d1e1cd3b46672d6ead</code></li><li><span>csv/job_openings.csv</span><code>bca19568d0ad8ea0daee354e603b86208012884e4e84bc2b50ca44071cb46f87</code></li><li><span>csv/applications.csv</span><code>68d3621e7bb49ac78fd8eecd6384253bf3ce1ba2e85cfea96883ac7ed0abbe37</code></li><li><span>csv/interviews.csv</span><code>242516f399d447ac57f02afddee998aca54e2691c4de15e608e8cfec70aeca83</code></li><li><span>csv/offers.csv</span><code>4a9c20275c0423c06abba75dc45aa00dfa516a1bc70971e3a603e9ee3d7aecbd</code></li><li><span>recruiting-pipeline.json</span><code>2f3987f38b0f98832e17611535600f0def9770afd68a464e152aa9398549d8ac</code></li><li><span>sql/postgres.sql</span><code>5140ef3eec635baa39732a91f964a79e1a289df0fd999219498b0cc147ea1017</code></li><li><span>sql/mysql.sql</span><code>beb3cf87fd3f4e5fa673a503d2bc342731c2c005a539b8d920551ef0d6f4e9fd</code></li><li><span>sql/mssql.sql</span><code>e590c439569f9cb68838af9b3d7c69e560b6cff79da5bd22479135f36be3ee36</code></li><li><span>sql/sqlite.sql</span><code>f5f0751678c070dc34a2363d18e5a53b4cb814db272a00a9751879de26dde123</code></li><li><span>prisma/seed.ts</span><code>18ea2c1c20505a238edaf62057cba381a027b04ebbab3d897226a9fc871f6a21</code></li><li><span>django/fixtures.json</span><code>ed218965bd513401a47f4cfd8bd02ef593246effc496e257011e9abe4481cd97</code></li></ul></details></section><section class="dataset-section" id="load"><h2>Load it</h2><div class="dataset-snippet"><h3>CSV</h3><pre><code>curl -O https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/csv/candidates.csv</code></pre><button type="button" aria-label="Copy the CSV command">Copy</button></div><div class="dataset-snippet"><h3>JSON</h3><pre><code>curl -O https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/recruiting-pipeline.json</code></pre><button type="button" aria-label="Copy the JSON command">Copy</button></div><div class="dataset-snippet"><h3>PostgreSQL</h3><pre><code>curl -sL https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/sql/postgres.sql | psql &quot;$DATABASE_URL&quot;</code></pre><button type="button" aria-label="Copy the PostgreSQL command">Copy</button></div><div class="dataset-snippet"><h3>MySQL</h3><pre><code>curl -sL https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/sql/mysql.sql | mysql -u root -p recruiting_pipeline</code></pre><button type="button" aria-label="Copy the MySQL command">Copy</button></div><div class="dataset-snippet"><h3>SQL Server</h3><pre><code>curl -sLo mssql.sql https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/sql/mssql.sql &amp;&amp; sqlcmd -S localhost -d recruiting_pipeline -i mssql.sql</code></pre><button type="button" aria-label="Copy the SQL Server command">Copy</button></div><div class="dataset-snippet"><h3>SQLite</h3><pre><code>curl -sL https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/sql/sqlite.sql | sqlite3 recruiting-pipeline.db</code></pre><button type="button" aria-label="Copy the SQLite command">Copy</button></div><div class="dataset-snippet"><h3>Prisma</h3><pre><code>curl -sLo prisma/seed.ts https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/prisma/seed.ts &amp;&amp; npx prisma db seed</code></pre><button type="button" aria-label="Copy the Prisma command">Copy</button></div><div class="dataset-snippet"><h3>Django</h3><pre><code>curl -sLo recruiting-pipeline.json https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/django/fixtures.json &amp;&amp; python manage.py loaddata recruiting-pipeline.json</code></pre><button type="button" aria-label="Copy the Django command">Copy</button></div><div class="dataset-snippet"><h3>pandas (Colab, Jupyter)</h3><pre><code>import pandas as pd

tables = {
    &quot;candidates&quot;: pd.read_csv(&quot;https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/csv/candidates.csv&quot;),
    &quot;job_openings&quot;: pd.read_csv(&quot;https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/csv/job_openings.csv&quot;),
    &quot;applications&quot;: pd.read_csv(&quot;https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/csv/applications.csv&quot;),
    &quot;interviews&quot;: pd.read_csv(&quot;https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/csv/interviews.csv&quot;),
    &quot;offers&quot;: pd.read_csv(&quot;https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v4/csv/offers.csv&quot;),
}</code></pre><button type="button" aria-label="Copy the pandas (Colab, Jupyter) command">Copy</button></div><div class="dataset-snippet"><h3>REST API</h3><pre><code>curl &quot;https://databasesample.com/api/v1/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/tables/candidates/rows?limit=100&quot;</code></pre><button type="button" aria-label="Copy the REST API command">Copy</button></div></section><section class="dataset-section" id="mock-api"><h2>As a REST API</h2><p>The same rows are served at<!-- --> <code>/mock/recruiting-pipeline/&lt;table&gt;</code>, with json-server’s filters, sorting, paging and relations — for a front end to call before its backend exists. No key, any origin.<!-- --> <a href="/mock-api/recruiting-pipeline">Its endpoints and examples</a>.</p></section><section class="dataset-section dataset-dictionary" id="schema"><h2>Tables and columns</h2><div><h3><a href="/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/t/job_openings">job_openings</a> <small>100<!-- --> <!-- -->rows</small></h3><p>Each row represents a job opening in the organization, linked to multiple applications from candidates.</p><div class="dataset-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Column</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Constraints</th><th scope="col">Values</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>id</code></td><td><code>integer</code></td><td>primary key</td><td>sequential id<!-- --> — <!-- -->Unique identifier for the job opening.</td></tr><tr><td><code>title</code></td><td><code>varchar(120)</code></td><td>nullable</td><td>title<!-- --> — <!-- -->Title of the job opening.</td></tr><tr><td><code>department</code></td><td><code>varchar(11)</code></td><td>—</td><td>one of Engineering, Marketing, Sales, HR<!-- --> — <!-- -->Department where the job opening is located.</td></tr><tr><td><code>created_at</code></td><td><code>timestamp</code></td><td>—</td><td>between 2022-01-01 and 2023-12-31<!-- --> — <!-- -->Date and time when the job opening was created.</td></tr><tr><td><code>status</code></td><td><code>varchar(6)</code></td><td>—</td><td>one of Open, Closed<!-- --> — <!-- -->Current status of the job opening.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div><h3><a href="/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/t/candidates">candidates</a> <small>200<!-- --> <!-- -->rows</small></h3><p>Each row represents a candidate applying for jobs, linked to their applications.</p><div class="dataset-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Column</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Constraints</th><th scope="col">Values</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>id</code></td><td><code>integer</code></td><td>primary key</td><td>sequential id<!-- --> — <!-- -->Unique identifier for the candidate.</td></tr><tr><td><code>full_name</code></td><td><code>varchar(120)</code></td><td>—</td><td>full name<!-- --> — <!-- -->Full name of the candidate.</td></tr><tr><td><code>email</code></td><td><code>varchar(120)</code></td><td>—</td><td>email<!-- --> — <!-- -->Email address of the candidate.</td></tr><tr><td><code>applied_at</code></td><td><code>timestamp</code></td><td>—</td><td>between 2022-01-01 and 2023-12-31<!-- --> — <!-- -->Date and time when the candidate applied.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div><h3><a href="/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/t/applications">applications</a> <small>506<!-- --> <!-- -->rows</small></h3><p>Each row represents an application made by a candidate for a job opening, linking candidates to job openings.</p><div class="dataset-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Column</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Constraints</th><th scope="col">Values</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>id</code></td><td><code>integer</code></td><td>primary key</td><td>sequential id<!-- --> — <!-- -->Unique identifier for the application.</td></tr><tr><td><code>candidate_id</code></td><td><code>integer</code></td><td>foreign key</td><td>references candidates.id<!-- --> — <!-- -->Reference to the candidate applying.</td></tr><tr><td><code>job_opening_id</code></td><td><code>integer</code></td><td>foreign key</td><td>references job_openings.id<!-- --> — <!-- -->Reference to the job opening applied for.</td></tr><tr><td><code>status</code></td><td><code>varchar(12)</code></td><td>—</td><td>one of Applied, Interviewing, Offer, Rejected<!-- --> — <!-- -->Current status of the application.</td></tr><tr><td><code>applied_at</code></td><td><code>timestamp</code></td><td>—</td><td>between 2022-01-01 and 2023-12-31<!-- --> — <!-- -->Date of application.</td></tr><tr><td><code>application_date</code></td><td><code>timestamp</code></td><td>—</td><td>between 2022-01-01 and 2023-12-31<!-- --> — <!-- -->Date when the application was submitted.</td></tr><tr><td><code>interview_count</code></td><td><code>integer</code></td><td>—</td><td>integer 0–3<!-- --> — <!-- -->Number of interviews conducted for this application.</td></tr><tr><td><code>candidate_rating</code></td><td><code>integer</code></td><td>nullable</td><td>integer 1–5<!-- --> — <!-- -->Rating given to the candidate by the interviewer; null if not rated.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div><h3><a href="/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/t/interviews">interviews</a> <small>822<!-- --> <!-- -->rows</small></h3><p>Each row captures an interview conducted for an application, linked to candidates and interviewers.</p><div class="dataset-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Column</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Constraints</th><th scope="col">Values</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>id</code></td><td><code>integer</code></td><td>primary key</td><td>sequential id<!-- --> — <!-- -->Unique identifier for the interview.</td></tr><tr><td><code>application_id</code></td><td><code>integer</code></td><td>foreign key</td><td>references applications.id<!-- --> — <!-- -->Reference to the application being interviewed.</td></tr><tr><td><code>interviewer</code></td><td><code>varchar(120)</code></td><td>nullable</td><td>full name<!-- --> — <!-- -->Name of the interviewer conducting the interview.</td></tr><tr><td><code>score</code></td><td><code>integer</code></td><td>nullable</td><td>integer 1–10<!-- --> — <!-- -->Score given by the interviewer for the interview.</td></tr><tr><td><code>interviewed_at</code></td><td><code>timestamp</code></td><td>—</td><td>between 2022-01-01 and 2023-12-31<!-- --> — <!-- -->Date and time of the interview.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div><h3><a href="/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/t/offers">offers</a> <small>155<!-- --> <!-- -->rows</small></h3><p>Each row represents an offer made to a candidate, linked to their application.</p><div class="dataset-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Column</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Constraints</th><th scope="col">Values</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>id</code></td><td><code>integer</code></td><td>primary key</td><td>sequential id<!-- --> — <!-- -->Unique identifier for the offer.</td></tr><tr><td><code>application_id</code></td><td><code>integer</code></td><td>foreign key</td><td>references applications.id<!-- --> — <!-- -->Reference to the application for which the offer is made.</td></tr><tr><td><code>offer_status</code></td><td><code>varchar(8)</code></td><td>—</td><td>one of Accepted, Declined<!-- --> — <!-- -->Status of the offer made to the candidate.</td></tr><tr><td><code>offered_at</code></td><td><code>timestamp</code></td><td>nullable</td><td>between 2022-01-01 and 2023-12-31<!-- --> — <!-- -->Date when the offer was made.</td></tr><tr><td><code>salary</code></td><td><code>numeric(14,2)</code></td><td>nullable</td><td>decimal 50000–200000<!-- --> — <!-- -->Salary offered to the candidate.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section class="dataset-section" id="diagram"><h2>Diagram</h2><p>The tables and the keys between them, as Mermaid: GitHub, GitLab and most documentation tools draw it from a fenced<!-- --> <code>mermaid</code> block, so it can sit beside the files in a repository.</p><div class="dataset-snippet"><h3>Mermaid</h3><pre><code>erDiagram
    %% Recruiting Pipeline: the tables its SQL files create.

    job_openings {
        integer id PK &quot;Unique identifier for the job opening.&quot;
        varchar title &quot;Title of the job opening.&quot;
        varchar department &quot;Department where the job opening is located.&quot;
        timestamp created_at &quot;Date and time when the job opening was created.&quot;
        varchar status &quot;Current status of the job opening.&quot;
    }

    candidates {
        integer id PK &quot;Unique identifier for the candidate.&quot;
        varchar full_name &quot;Full name of the candidate.&quot;
        varchar email &quot;Email address of the candidate.&quot;
        timestamp applied_at &quot;Date and time when the candidate applied.&quot;
    }

    applications {
        integer id PK &quot;Unique identifier for the application.&quot;
        integer candidate_id FK &quot;Reference to the candidate applying.&quot;
        integer job_opening_id FK &quot;Reference to the job opening applied for.&quot;
        varchar status &quot;Current status of the application.&quot;
        timestamp applied_at &quot;Date of application.&quot;
        timestamp application_date &quot;Date when the application was submitted.&quot;
        integer interview_count &quot;Number of interviews conducted for this application.&quot;
        integer candidate_rating &quot;Rating given to the candidate by the interviewer; null if not rated.&quot;
    }

    interviews {
        integer id PK &quot;Unique identifier for the interview.&quot;
        integer application_id FK &quot;Reference to the application being interviewed.&quot;
        varchar interviewer &quot;Name of the interviewer conducting the interview.&quot;
        integer score &quot;Score given by the interviewer for the interview.&quot;
        timestamp interviewed_at &quot;Date and time of the interview.&quot;
    }

    offers {
        integer id PK &quot;Unique identifier for the offer.&quot;
        integer application_id FK &quot;Reference to the application for which the offer is made.&quot;
        varchar offer_status &quot;Status of the offer made to the candidate.&quot;
        timestamp offered_at &quot;Date when the offer was made.&quot;
        numeric salary &quot;Salary offered to the candidate.&quot;
    }

    applications ||--|{ interviews : &quot;has&quot;
    applications ||--|{ offers : &quot;has&quot;
    candidates ||--|{ applications : &quot;has&quot;
    job_openings ||--|{ applications : &quot;has&quot;
</code></pre><button type="button" aria-label="Copy the Mermaid command">Copy</button></div></section><section class="dataset-section" id="as-code"><h2>The tables as code</h2><p>The same tables, with the names and types the SQL files create, as models or types for your project.</p><ul class="schema-downloads-list"><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=prisma" download="">Prisma</a></li><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=drizzle" download="">Drizzle</a></li><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=typeorm" download="">TypeORM</a></li><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=sequelize" download="">Sequelize</a></li><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=django" download="">Django</a></li><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=sqlalchemy" download="">SQLAlchemy</a></li><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=eloquent" download="">Laravel</a></li><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=laravel-migration" download="">Laravel migration</a></li><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=efcore" download="">EF Core</a></li><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=jpa" download="">JPA (Hibernate)</a></li><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=gorm" download="">GORM</a></li><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=activerecord" download="">Rails</a></li><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=typescript" download="">TypeScript types</a></li><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=zod" download="">Zod</a></li><li><a href="/api/datasets/model?slug=recruiting-pipeline&amp;format=pydantic" download="">Pydantic</a></li></ul></section><section class="dataset-section" id="versions"><h2>Earlier versions</h2><p>This is version <!-- -->4<!-- -->. Nothing published is overwritten: each earlier version&#x27;s files stay at their own address, and its manifest lists them with their checksums.</p><ul><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v3/manifest.json">Version <!-- -->3<!-- --> manifest</a></li><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v2/manifest.json">Version <!-- -->2<!-- --> manifest</a></li><li><a href="https://database-sample-website.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/datasets/recruiting-pipeline/v1/manifest.json">Version <!-- -->1<!-- --> manifest</a></li></ul></section><section class="dataset-section" id="preview"><h2>Preview</h2><p class="p-sm">The first ten rows of each table, exactly as the files have them.</p><div><h3>candidates</h3><div class="dataset-table-wrap"><table><caption class="visually-hidden">First rows of candidates</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">id</th><th scope="col">full_name</th><th scope="col">email</th><th scope="col">applied_at</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Felix Mendes</td><td><a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="cea8aba2a7b6e0a3aba0aaabbd8eabb6afa3bea2abe0a1bca9">[email&#160;protected]</a></td><td>2022-08-12 22:20:15</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Hannah Flores</td><td><a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="d5bdb4bbbbb4bdfbb3b9baa7b0a695b0adb4b8a5b9b0fbbaa7b2">[email&#160;protected]</a></td><td>2023-08-13 10:05:46</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Rosa Hansen</td><td><a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="0b7964786a25636a65786e654b6e736a667b676e25656e7f">[email&#160;protected]</a></td><td>2023-02-12 16:14:41</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Nadia Novak</td><td><a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="2c424d48454d0242435a4d476c49544d415c4049024f4341">[email&#160;prote